                            <comment id="15167116" author="vozerov" created="Thu, 25 Feb 2016 11:50:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ilya, my comments:&lt;br/&gt;
1) absMap/BALANCE: you should create version-dependent job, then find balanced node and then &lt;em&gt;optionally&lt;/em&gt; fallback to old job if selected node is &amp;lt;1.6. For now you have 2 job allocations in the most common case.&lt;br/&gt;
2) outMap: same as p.1&lt;br/&gt;
3) T8/T9/T10.map: same as p.1. You can simply all these usages into a dedicated method to avoid duplication.&lt;br/&gt;
4) T9.map: same as p.1.&lt;br/&gt;
5) C1V2/C1MLAV2/C2V2/C2MLAV2/C4V2/C4MLAV2 - raw writer/reader should be used instead.&lt;br/&gt;
6) Are we sure that all these classes are serialized using binary marshaler? As I remember, there is some logic which will write all system classes in &quot;optimized&quot; form, no?&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="15167148" author="ilantukh" created="Thu, 25 Feb 2016 12:33:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed, relaunched tests.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
